A||||3||WisconsinGT||AUTOMATIC TRANSMISSION SHIFT KIT ||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-25-2000||12:15 AM||||Has anyone bought the auto. shift kit the Fiero Store sells? If so, did you have to take out the trasmission to put it in? Can you share with me the process for installation? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||08-25-2000||03:05 AM||||My shift kit was bought thru IRM but I think it is the same as the Fiero Store (TransGo is the brand name) No the trans does not need to be removed. The directions that came with mine were very well written. Basically you drop the pan and filter, then remove the valve body and put in the new parts. Took me about 2 hours to do it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||08-25-2000||06:27 AM||||I purchased the trans kit from the Fiero store. The shift kit didn't make the car shift as radical as I thought, but does allow for a better 3rd to 2nd down shift. I installed it in a rebuilt 3.33 trans from a 87 that I got from the salvage yard. I put it in before I installed the tranny. It looks like it can be installed while in the car. What a mess I had taking the old trans out, forgot to drain it first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Eric<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||80's BOY||08-25-2000||04:04 PM||||the kit i bought from the fiero store was called "mr. shift". the instructions were very clear, and installation is fairly simple for the mechanically inclined. it helped some, but not drastic results like i thought. i installed it with the tranny in the car. it was not that difficult in my opinion. good luck!!||||reg||14
